WEBVTT

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.660
Yuichi!

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.500
Kokorogi!

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.920
Manabu? Or not.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.180
I'll serve as MC for this special 
edition of Tomodachi Game.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.320
The name's Kuroki.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.170
Friendship

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.320
thief

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.320
parent and child crooks

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.080
All right, I'll explain the rules 
of the Weak Win Game one more time.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:09.930
<b>Episode 12: What's Most Important to Me Is...</b>

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.650
<b>Episode 12: What's Most Important to Me Is...</b>

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.490
Hold it! I'm not going to listen to a thing 
you say until you let Kokorogi go!

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.990
Is that so?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.830
You piece of—

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.450
Hey, now. Do you understand
 the position you're in right now?

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:32.620
If you want, I could expose that secret 
of yours that you've never told anyone.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.810
You think...

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.960
you know <i>that</i> much about me?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.390
Huh? You want me to spill, for real?

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.260
If Yutori-chan hears about it, saving her 
will be the least of your worries.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.930
Are you listening <i>now</i>, Katagiri Yuichi-kun?

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.840
Yuichi-kun will be subjected to
 three rounds of physical pain.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.940
If he can endure the pain, 
we'll let him and his friend both go.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.960
But a game doesn't test their friendship

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.930
wouldn't be much of a 
Tomodachi Game, would it?

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.060
So, there's one way for Yuichi-kun 
to escape the violence.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.660
What?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.950
It's you.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.040
You can take the pain instead of Yuichi.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.540
Yutori-chan gets to choose 
which one of them suffers.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.370
The point here is that 
if Yutori-chan chooses herself,

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.050
her pain will be lighter than Yuichi-kun's.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.040
Hey, Kokorogi—

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.970
Ah, but Yuichi-kun isn't allowed to talk.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.720
If Yuichi-kun speaks while she's 
deciding, they both suffer.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.350
Ultimately, Yutori-chan is the one 
who'll decide who gets hurt.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:37.300
Basically, it's a question of whether or not 
she's selfless enough to protect Yuichi-kun.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.110
<b></b>Selflessness

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.610
Okay, let's go ahead with 
the first round of pain.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.270
You'll get punched by our very 
own Hercules, Goriki-kun. Yeah.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.380
If Yutori-chan chooses herself, 
she gets one hit.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.120
If she chooses Yuichi-kun, 
he gets three hits.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:57.460
By the way, Goriki-kun 
is just as strong as he seems.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.630
For a little girl like you, even 
one punch could rearrange your face.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.090
You have five seconds to choose.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:10.600
If you don't choose in that time, 
Yuichi-kun will be selected automatically.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.730
Okay, five, four, three...

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.570
I...

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.360
two, one.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.900
Yu-Yuichi?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.570
Aw, I should've said you can't move, either.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.040
But, oh well.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.490
In honor of Yuichi-kun's beautiful 
self-sacrifice this first round,

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.690
I'll let you have it.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.210
Yutori-chan, take a close look.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.210
What happens next is
 the result of your actions.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.610
First hit!

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.930
Second hit!

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:46.930
Last one!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.670
<i>Man, I keep getting beat up these days.</i>

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.560
<i>At least this guy didn't hit 
as hard as that gorilla Captain.</i>

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.440
Are you okay, Yuichi?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.320
I'm... I mean... um...

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.780
I can take the next one. 
I'm so sorry, Yuichi.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.780
There you go! Now that's 
what I call friendship!

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.980
So we're going with Yutori-chan 
for the next round of pain, right?

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:11.910
Yeah.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.410
Okay. Put your hand right here.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.290
The pain this time is 
fingernail removal. Yeah.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.250
You think you can handle it, Yutori-chan?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.160
Oh, right.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.830
This time I'll give you the chance 
to switch to Yuichi-kun, if you want.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:26.930
But...

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.880
If Yuichi-kun does it, 
he'll lose three fingernails.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.430
He'd get three times 
the pain you would.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.320
So? Which one will it be?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.820
All right, here we go.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.910
Yuichi!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.870
W-What should I do, Yuichi?!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.870
It hurts! It really, really hurts!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.590
You heard her, Yuichi-kun.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:58.460
Oh? You mad, Yuichi-kun?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.620
Or maybe just a little scared, huh?

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.840
Stop talking. Shut up and do it.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:07.420
Sounds good! As requested sir, 
I'll pull them all at once!

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.520
One!

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.060
Two!

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.510
Three!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.540
How was that?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.830
Yuichi-kun, how you feelin', buddy?

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.000
How you feelin', Yutori-chan?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.360
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry...

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.240
Hey, you guys...

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.790
Why is this piece of shit your leader?

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:29.860
Huh?

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.240
Do you see anything good in him at all?

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.620
Any way you look at it, 
Goriki-kun is a stronger fighter.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.870
As for this perverted, sadistic ass,

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.640
even his face looks like a nasty snake.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.500
You don't get it at all, do you?

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.840
The most important thing 
for a leader isn't strength.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.720
It's this. <i>This!</i> I'm the
 smartest guy in the room.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.580
You can't raise a finger 
against me now, right?

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.480
I'm the only one here who can pull that off.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:02.350
And I've got guts. No matter 
what happens, nothing shakes me.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.860
Last of all, and this is the most important,

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.360
I never sell my friends out.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.150
Okay.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.280
So you have brains, you have guts, 
and you don't betray your friends,

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.240
and that qualifies you to be leader. Right?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.000
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.280
Let's get back to the game, then.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:24.000
But before that, let's mix 
things up for the last one.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
If Yutori-chan chooses herself,

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.850
well make her dance totally naked!

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:30.880
Yeah!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.580
I guess it's more like 
emotional pain this time.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.890
It'd be damn humiliating to have this many 
guys drooling over every inch of your body.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:42.900
But no one here wants to see
 Yuichi-kun naked, so if he gets picked,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.150
I'll gouge his hand with this 
three times instead.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.970
I'll give you a minute this time. 
You should talk it over.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.950
Ain't much to talk about, though.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.410
It's either the girl gettin' humiliated,

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:58.450
or the guy gettin' hurt real 
bad three times over.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.250
Is there really any room for discussion?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.710
You... You can decide, Yuichi.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.570
Holy shit! You serious, Yutori-chan?!

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.750
Shouldn't you volunteer this round?!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.660
Kokorogi, tell me how you honestly feel.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:15.760
B-But, I... I know I should 
do it this time, I know that...

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.510
but I can't decide. 
I can't get the words out!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.090
Five seconds left!

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.180
So, y-you decide, Yuichi!

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.750
Four, three,

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.470
I promise to do whatever you say!

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.470
two, one...

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.730
Okay.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.190
I'll do it.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.570
Oh, you're bad! 
You're the worst, Yutori-chan!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.610
Can't handle anything, 
can't make up your damn mind...

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.820
You're the weakest of the weak, Yutori-chan.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.620
But thanks to all that, you got
 away without a scratch.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.100
The weak really <i>do</i> win, Yutori-chan!

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:48.960
Let's get started.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.050
I won't even tie your hand down. 
Show us what you're made of!

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.240
Even tough guy Yuichi-kun 
screamed that time!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.440
Are you hearing this, Yutori-chan?

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.660
Last one!

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:10.650
Nice work! And that concludes our 
special edition of the Tomodachi Game.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.050
You're free to go home.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:16.700
Though I doubt you'll feel like 
leaving together after this.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.030
Yeah, I'm definitely pissed.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.320
I seriously snapped. 
I haven't been this angry in a long time.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.710
I know, right? Yutori-chan 
really is a piece of shit.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.970
Hey now, don't get it twisted.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.790
Huh?

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:36.010
This stupid child's play won't 
make me forget who's to blame.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:39.470
My anger is all for you, asshole! <i>Kuroki!</i>

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:43.510
Don't worry, Kokorogi. 
I'm not mad at you at all.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.600
This is a play that kidnappers often use.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.110
They say, "If you don't accept my demands, 
the hostages will get hurt."

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:53.940
Then the kidnappers manipulate 
the people who refuse their demands

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.360
into doing something bad.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.100
But if you think about it, the real bad guys

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.380
are the kidnappers 
who started the whole thing.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.370
Like these jerks here.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.000
You're only a victim. There's no
 reason for you to feel guilty.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.210
It's basically my fault you were 
targeted in the first place.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.090
I'm sorry, Kokorogi.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:17.010
I'm so sorry, Yuichi! I... I...

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.050
You aren't scared of me anymore?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.160
I don't know what you were like in the past,

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.960
but you've been really, really kind to me,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.400
so I'm... I'm going to trust 
the Yuichi I know. I trust you!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.580
All right. Thanks, Kokorogi.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.400
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.970
Can you get back by yourself? 
I have unfinished business here.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.660
Then I'll stay, too.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.430
You sure?

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:49.620
You'll end up seeing something scary.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.000
It's okay. I've made up my mind 
to trust you, Yuichi.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.630
All right. I'll get started, then.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:57.950
Hey, Kuroki-kun.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.880
You wanna play another game with me?

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:07.390
A game?

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.810
Are you kidding? 
What would I get out of that?

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.560
10 million yen.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.560
<b>10 Million Yen</b>

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:17.400
If you win, I'll give you 
10 million yen in cash.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.410
10 million?!

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.180
Seriously?!

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.950
Then let me play!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:25.420
C'mon, man. I doubt you have 
that much in the first place.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.160
Huh? You said you knew about my past, right?

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:33.680
Then you must know I have more
 than that in loose change.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.540
Ah, yeah, sure.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.420
Fine, then. Tell me about this game.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.380
It's simple. Rock Paper Scissors.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.690
Rock Paper Scissors?

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.390
One round of Rock Paper Scissors.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.850
If you win, you get 10 million yen. 
If you lose, how about...

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.910
I cut off your fingers.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.680
If you throw paper and lose,
 I'll cut off all five.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.180
If you throw scissors and lose, 
I'll cut off two.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:12:00.610
If you throw rock, I won't cut off any. 
So you risk nothing.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.950
Let's call it Rock Paper Fingers.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.110
<b>Rock Paper Fingers</b>

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:03.320
<b>Rock Paper Fingers</b>

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:03.950
<b>Rock Paper Fingers</b>

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:03.950
<b>Rock Paper Fingers</b>

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.320
Doesn't that sound like fun?

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:10.680
Ah, but you can relax. 
You've got a huge advantage.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.710
'Cause I can only throw rock 
or paper with this hand.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:17.340
Let's do it.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.660
First one is rock—

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.550
Just wait a second! 
I didn't say I was gonna—

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.720
Huh?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.020
Even with that <i>massive</i> advantage, 
you aren't gonna play?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.180
No way. Oh man, don't tell me...

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.060
you're scared?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.390
Fine! If Kuroki wins,

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:37.650
I'll give everyone here one 
million yen each. As a bonus!

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:38.520
Seriously?!

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.110
One million each!

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.110
Wahoo!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:42.670
This game gives Kuroki a massive advantage!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:46.110
Would someone with brains 
<i>and</i> guts really turn this down?!

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.120
Let's give your loyal leader 
a little support, here!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.640
Yeah! All right!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:57.000
Do it! Do it!

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.620
Getting interesting, huh, Kuroki?

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.240
You little shit.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.340
Fine.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.380
I'll play your damn game! Bleh!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.380
<b>Bleh!</b>

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:07.470
<i>Yeah, I'll play your game. 
There's no way I can lose.</i>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
<b>Win</b>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
<b>Win</b>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
<b>Win</b>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
High <b>Risk</b>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
No <b>Risk</b>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:16.730
Medium <b>Risk</b>

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.650
<i>If you lay out the moves, 
this is what you get.</i>

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:14.530
<i>To win against the low-risk rock, 
you need to use the high-risk paper.</i>

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.730
<i>It's a surprisingly smart game.</i>

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.360
<i>But here's the main point:</i>

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.110
<i>He can only throw rock or paper.</i>

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.970
<i>If I throw paper, there's no way I'll lose.</i>

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.610
<b>Tie</b>

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.610
<b>Win</b>

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.610
<i>At the very worst, it'll be a tie.</i>

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.140
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.360
Hey. What happens if we tie?

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:36.120
Tie? I really doubt that'll ever happen.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.580
But if it does, we'll just end 
the game with no penalty.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:43.800
<i>No penalty? Is he hoping for a tie?</i>

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.140
<i>He must know I'll throw paper.</i>

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:49.550
<i>Since he can only throw rock or paper, 
his only choice is paper...</i>

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.980
<i>So if I throw scissors, I'll win?!</i>

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:56.180
<i>Is that what you expected 
me to think, idiot?</i>

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.180
<i>Scissors do have a good chance of winning,</i>

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:02.620
<i>but there's also a chance they might lose.</i>

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:06.180
<i>I can't reach out and grab 
the prize dangling in front of me</i>

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:10.950
<i>if there's even a 0.1% chance of losing!</i>

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.620
You're planning to throw paper, aren't you?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.000
So what if I was?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
I don't really care. It's just...

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.960
that would show us exactly 
how pathetic you are.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:24.850
You tryin' to taunt me?

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.160
You ain't gonna make me change my throw!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.800
Your only choice is to throw paper anyway!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.010
Nope, I'm not going to throw paper.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.100
Huh?

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.550
Let's do this!

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:36.140
First one is rock,

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:40.610
<i>Don't be fooled! If he really doesn't 
throw paper, all he's got is rock!</i>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.940
Rock, paper...

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.490
<i>So I've gotta throw paper!</i>

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.780
<i>Paper, paper, paper!</i>

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.280
Scissors.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.070
<i>H-He...</i>

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.070
<i>His left hand?!</i>

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.400
You lying piece of shit!

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:57.000
That isn't what we agreed!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.460
The hell it isn't!

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.820
I told you I wouldn't throw paper.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.320
That's not what I mean!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:07.220
You said you could only use rock or paper!

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.630
Yeah, with my right hand.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:13.260
But no one said I couldn't use my left.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.440
You think I'm gonna fall 
for that bullshit excuse?!

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.160
Guys! Teach this guy a lesson!

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.160
Uh? Huh?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.070
What about the game?

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.600
It doesn't count!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.890
I told you to get him!

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.780
Stop right there!

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.910
Restrain them all!

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.780
Ugh!

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:33.940
What?!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.240
Gah!

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.330
Like hell, you bitch!

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.380
Ow, ow, ow!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.400
Whoa!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:47.630
The Tomodachi Game management 
will be taking over from here!

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.280
Hmph!

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.510
Cheers!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.810
That was miraculous timing, Tenji.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:57.180
Sorry. I got here a little while ago, 
but they wouldn't let me barge in.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.920
You're the leader of this group, correct?

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:03.810
And the man impersonating 
the Tomodachi Game?

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.220
W-Why?

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:08.010
I followed Yuichi's instructions 
and called the real ones.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:08.730
Huh?!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.940
<b></b>Unknown Caller

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.940
<b></b>In Call

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.360
Yuichi got a bad feeling 
about that first call.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.330
Even though you tried to act like Manabu,

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:19.740
<b>Bessatsu Shonen 
Magazine</b>

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:17.320
you sounded a lot trashier 
than the real one.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:25.250
So I contacted the real ones and 
gave them the location you told us.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.380
Now you're coming with me.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:31.170
I'll show you what happens to
 someone who impersonates us.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.300
Hold on. I can't let you snatch my prize.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:37.760
I've still got important 
business with this guy.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:42.650
So, Kuroki-kun, you haven't forgotten 
about your promise to me, right?

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.520
P-Promise?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.090
You threw paper and lost.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.080
You owe me five fingers!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.900
I... I said I wasn't buying that!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.200
This is bullshit!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:58.060
Would you mind hurrying it up, then?

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.580
We're busy too, you know.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.250
Make up your mind, Kuroki.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.460
Shit! Get your shoe off me!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.970
So, which finger goes first?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.250
Hey! Someone stop this psycho asshole!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.650
Oh, c'mon.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:15.720
If you won't choose, 
how about I pick for you?

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.970
Which finger should go first?

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:27.080
Please stop!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.400
Oh. That's right.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.080
I can stop if you want.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.440
Y-You can?

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.690
As long as you pick one 
of your friends to take your place.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:38.950
But I'll only cut off one of their fingers.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.800
H-Hey! You guys hear that?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.130
If it isn't me, you'll get off 
with one-fifth the injury!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.950
Yeah, someone come take my place!

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:47.420
Hey, c'mon. We're all pals, right?

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:50.090
Someone step up and take it! Now! C'mon!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:56.220
Sons of bitches! You dumb 
assholes won't follow my orders?!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.840
It's five fingers! <i>Five!</i>

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.740
That's worth more than <i>one</i> 
of your shitty fingers!

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.900
What the hell, you freakin' cowards?!

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:05.700
You gonna cry over one 
goddamn finger?! Huh?!

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:06.980
I won't forget this, you assholes—

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.270
Kuroki.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.050
I-I'm sorry! Please forgive me this time!

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:12.180
I'll never impersonate the 
Tomodachi Game again!

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:14.650
Don't worry. The game has already ended.

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:17.740
Katagiri Yuichi has passed out.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.570
Yuichi!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.060
Yuichi! Yuichi!

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:30.530
God damn it! I still don't buy it.

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:33.480
Pretending he won after 
that childish trick...

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:36.870
Childish? You don't have a clue, do you?

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:42.260
Under the rules for Rock Paper Fingers, 
what hand did you think was superior?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.870
Obviously either paper, which couldn't lose,

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:46.610
or scissors, which had a good chance to win.

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.880
Right. Because of what he said.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:49.770
Huh?

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.650
'Cause I can only throw rock 
or paper with this hand.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:57.260
But that was exactly Katagiri Yuichi's plan.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:00.160
He intended to use scissors from the start.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:04.980
Given that, how could he make absolutely 
sure not to end in a tie or lose?

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:08.960
To make me think rock wasn't an option...

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.500
Yes. What he, what Katagiri Yuichi did,

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:17.590
was use a truly cold and calculating 
method that ensured he wouldn't lose.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:21.580
Even, even if that's true, 
he ran out of strength

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:24.980
and I got away with all my fingers 
and didn't lose a thing!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.740
You really <i>are</i> a complete idiot.

00:19:29.740 --> 00:19:30.600
Huh?

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:36.360
The game revealed three facts about you, 
and made you lose one very big thing.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:40.330
It revealed that you have 
no brains, have no guts,

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.590
and that you <i>easily</i> betray your friends.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:47.490
As expected, when I talked to the other 
members about dealing with you,

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:50.330
they said, "That guy means 
nothing to us anymore."

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.150
"Do whatever you want with him."

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.490
In just one game of Rock Paper Scissors,

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:58.350
he destroyed all of your 
connections to other people.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.380
Yuichi! Are you okay? Hang on!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.350
Yuichi! Yuichi!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:07.350
Yuichi! Yuichi!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.950
Who are you, exactly?

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.080
I'm the girl Yuichi took for a fling.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.830
Move over!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:13.930
Meow!

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:15.240
What's happened here?

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.230
It's amazing he stayed conscious 
after losing this much blood.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.700
Emergency transport! Stretcher! Hurry!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:21.740
Right!

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.240
Are you going to save him?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.940
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:27.370
During the game, you're our products.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.270
We can't let him die 
a boring death like this.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:35.040
As long as you save him, I don't care! 
We'll stay by his side!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:38.400
Wow, Tenji. You guys sure are good to him.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.090
Of course we are! Yuichi's our friend!

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.050
Yeah!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:46.300
In that case, don't you have another friend 
who needs you even more right now?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:50.970
That's right. Shibe Makoto, the murderer.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:56.500
If you participate in the next game, 
you might be able to save Shibe!

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.060
Really? In that case—

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.190
However, you'll get saddled 
with another 500 million in debt.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:02.100
What—

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:03.440
F-Five hundred million?!

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:06.820
Poor Shibe got stuck with 
a 500 million yen debt

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.390
that was left when his father died.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:14.110
So, what will you choose? 
Your money or your friend?

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.250
Yuichi!

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:19.990
Yuichi!

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:23.430
You've got to go!

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.560
Yuichi!

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:29.600
Are we going to leave the game like this, 
before we find out the truth?

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.850
Yuichi!

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:35.640
The most important thing 
to me isn't money, anyway.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.000
Friends...

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:41.370
Yuichi!

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:43.110
Yuichi! Yuichi!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.640
Looks like he won't be able to participate.

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:46.930
Take him away.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:48.280
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.620
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:53.870
It's all right, Yuichi.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.630
I promise to bring Shibe home.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.380
Me, too.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:02.130
I'm still scared and hurt 
and I wish I could run away,

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.780
but I'm done being a stranger!

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:06.130
Kokorogi-san.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:11.390
There was so much going on, 
I didn't really know who I could trust,

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:17.000
but Yuichi risked his life to protect me, 
so I decided that I would only trust him.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.090
So... So that's why...

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:22.110
Since I know Yuichi has faith in you, 
I'll go with you, Mikasa-kun.

00:22:29.500 --> 00:22:31.660
Silence! Silence!

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:35.620
Bring the defendant Shibe Makoto
 into the courtroom.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.390
The charge is patricide.

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:47.670
I hereby begin the fourth game, 
Friendship Guilt Court!

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:49.930
<b>Friendship Guilt Courthouse</b>
